From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:00:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 43/66] mac80211: ath11k: don't warn when a country leaves a
 radio without channels

ath11k patch 112 (for upstream), B107: on a C-360, "iw reg set CA" left
the 6 GHz-only QCN9074 with no enabled channel, and ath11k's channel
list update hit a WARN_ON() and failed with -EINVAL. A domain with no
channel for a radio is not a driver fault: there is no list to send,
nothing can start on the radio meanwhile, and the next domain that
enables a channel sends the list again. Log it at debug level and
return 0, as ath12k already does.

Bump PKG_RELEASE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile              |  2 +-
 ...untry-leaves-a-pdev-without-channels.patch | 51 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 52 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100755 package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/112-wifi-ath11k-don-t-warn-when-a-country-leaves-a-pdev-without-channels.patch

diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile b/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile
index ca360f55f4..1c78350dce 100644
--- a/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ PKG_NAME:=mac80211
 
 PKG_SOURCE_VERSION:=7.2
 PKG_VERSION:=$(subst -,_,$(PKG_SOURCE_VERSION))
-PKG_RELEASE:=22
+PKG_RELEASE:=23
 PKG_LICENSE:=GPL-2.0-only
 PKG_LICENSE_FILES:=COPYING
 
diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/112-wifi-ath11k-don-t-warn-when-a-country-leaves-a-pdev-without-channels.patch b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/112-wifi-ath11k-don-t-warn-when-a-country-leaves-a-pdev-without-channels.patch
new file mode 100755
index 0000000000..a982ef1515
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/112-wifi-ath11k-don-t-warn-when-a-country-leaves-a-pdev-without-channels.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH ath-next] wifi: ath11k: don't warn when a country leaves a
+ pdev without channels
+
+ath11k_reg_update_chan_list() hits a WARN_ON() and returns -EINVAL when
+none of the pdev's channels is enabled. Userspace can reach that by
+setting a country. On an Arista C-360, whose QCN9074 is a 6 GHz-only
+pdev, "iw reg set CA" left that wiphy with no enabled channel, and the
+driver-initiated regulatory notifier then warned:
+
+  WARNING: ... at drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c:146 ath11k_reg_update_chan_list+0x368/0x3c0
+  ath11k_pci 0000:01:00.0: failed to update channel list: -22
+
+A domain with no channel for a pdev is not a driver fault. There is no
+list to send (ath11k_wmi_send_scan_chan_list_cmd() sends nothing for
+zero channels anyway), no vdev can start on the pdev meanwhile, and the
+next domain that enables a channel sends the whole list again. ath12k
+already treats this case as a debug message.
+
+Log it at debug level and return 0. That also covers
+ath11k_mac_op_start(), which ignores the return value but hits the same
+WARN_ON() when the radio is started in such a domain.
+
+Fixes: d5c65159f289 ("ath11k: driver for Qualcomm IEEE 802.11ax devices")
+Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
+Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
+---
+ drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c | 12 ++++++++++--
+ 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
+
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/reg.c
+@@ -143,8 +143,16 @@ int ath11k_reg_update_chan_list(struct ath11k *ar, bool wait)
+ 		}
+ 	}
+
+-	if (WARN_ON(!num_channels))
+-		return -EINVAL;
++	/* A regulatory domain can leave a pdev with no usable channel, as
++	 * one without 6 GHz rules leaves a 6 GHz-only radio. There is no
++	 * list to send then; the domain that enables a channel again sends it.
++	 */
++	if (!num_channels) {
++		ath11k_dbg(ar->ab, ATH11K_DBG_REG,
++			   "no enabled channel on pdev %u, channel list not sent\n",
++			   ar->pdev->pdev_id);
++		return 0;
++	}
+
+ 	params = kzalloc_flex(*params, ch_param, num_channels);
+ 	if (!params)
